From 1937c57d3c85ddef1fbb6d3e3817a644e50af941 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 23:12:12 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(spec-decode): DSpark draft trace for offline policy
 replay

Choosing a DSpark draft count, verification rule or confidence
calibration takes one boot per arm, and boot-to-boot noise hides small
differences. At temperature 0 the committed stream is the target's greedy
output, so a draft token is correct exactly when it equals the committed
token at its position, whether or not it was verified. A run that records
every draft and its confidence therefore prices every verification cap
and rule offline against the profiled cost tables.

With SPARK3_DSPARK_TRACE=<path>, TP rank 0 appends one JSON line per
request per step: tokens sampled, drafts verified from the previous step,
and the drafts and raw confidences proposed for the next step. It copies
GPU tensors to the host each step, so it is for replay runs only, never
for timing. Off unless the variable is set; output is unchanged.
